#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:18
msgid "1.1 Configuring the Blynk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:20
msgid "In this chapter we create a Blynk account, a template and a device, and then copy the three lines that go at the top of every project sketch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:25
msgid "The Blynk.Console interface is updated from time to time. The screenshots below were taken in 2026. If a button has moved, look for the **field name** (such as `AUTH TOKEN`) instead of the exact button position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:30
msgid "1. Create an account"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:32
msgid "Go to `BLYNK <https://blynk.io/>`_ and click **Sign Up** in the upper right corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:42
msgid "Enter your email address, tick the agreement box and click **Sign Up**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:52
msgid "Open the activation link in your mailbox, then create a password."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:63
msgid "2. Enable Developer Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:65
msgid "Blynk has to know that you are the person **building** the device and not the end user. Only a user in **Developer Mode** can create templates, dashboards and devices, which is everything this kit needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:69
msgid "Click **My Profile** in the upper right corner of the Blynk.Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:71
msgid "Make sure the **Developer Mode** switch is set to **ON**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:73
msgid "The first account of an organization is a developer by default, but on some accounts the switch has to be turned on by hand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:78
msgid "If the sidebar has no **Developer Zone** and no **+ New Template** button, the **Developer Mode** switch is still off. Turn it on and the menu items appear - no need to sign out or create another account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:84
msgid "**Developer Mode** is a setting of your account, not a paid feature. The free plan already allows it. What the free plan limits is the number of devices and the number of messages per day, so for a classroom it is usually enough to create one template and reuse it for every board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:90
msgid "3. Create a template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:92
msgid "After signing in you will see the **Blynk.Console**. Open **Developer Zone** in the left sidebar, then **My Templates**, and click **+ New Template**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:107
msgid "Fill in the template form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:109
msgid "**NAME**: `Ultimate Sensor`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:110
msgid "**HARDWARE**: **ESP32**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:111
msgid "**CONNECTION TYPE**: **WiFi**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:119
msgid "**HARDWARE** is only a label that Blynk uses to suggest example code. Both **ESP32** and **ESP8266** work with the projects in this kit; the screenshot above uses **ESP32**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:123
msgid "Click **Done** when finished."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:130
msgid "4. Create a device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:132
msgid "A template on its own has **no** auth token - a device has. Every device you create gets its own token."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:135
msgid "In the left sidebar click **Devices**, then **+ New Device**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:145
msgid "Choose **Create New**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:155
msgid "Select the template you just created, give the device a name, and click **Create**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:165
msgid "A **New Device Created!** window pops up with the three lines you need."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:173
msgid "If you close that window, the same information is always available in **Devices** -> your device -> **Developer Tools**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:181
msgid "5. Put them at the top of the sketch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:191
msgid "Copy them **exactly**. A single wrong character and the board will never connect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:194
msgid "6. Install the Blynk library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:196
msgid "In the Arduino IDE open **Library Manager**, search for `blynk` and install **Blynk 1.4.0**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:205
msgid "The sketches in this kit use `BlynkSimpleShieldEsp8266`, which needs a **second** library called **BlynkESP8266** (it provides `ESP8266_Lib.h`). It is **not** in Library Manager and has to be installed manually:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:209
msgid "Open https://github.com/vshymanskyy/BlynkESP8266"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:210
msgid "Click **Code -> Download ZIP**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:211
msgid "In the Arduino IDE choose **Sketch -> Include Library -> Add .ZIP Library**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:212
msgid "Restart the IDE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/blynk_start/02-iot_blynk_config.rst:214
msgid "See :doc:`03-iot_add_lib` for more details."
msgstr ""
